    </ul>
    <p style="margin-top:.75rem;margin-bottom:0;color:#63553F;">Airalo's code is the best public one we've verified, since Airalo runs a referral program (Airmoney) rather than a central affiliate discount, which is why so many different codes circulate for it. Saily's HELLOSAILY applies storewide and isn't tied to a first purchase.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Is Airalo or Saily the Right Pick</h2>
  <div class="decision-grid">
    <div class="decision-card decision-card--primary">
      <h3>Go with Airalo if&hellip;</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You want the widest selection of individual country eSIMs</li>
        <li>You're comfortable tracking a data meter for the lowest possible base price</li>
        <li>You don't care about a bundled VPN or ad blocker</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="decision-card decision-card--secondary">
      <h3>Go with Saily if&hellip;</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>You'd normally pay for a VPN or ad blocker separately when traveling anyway</li>
        <li>Multi-country trip where you don't want a new eSIM at every border</li>
        <li>You want the slightly lower per-GB price</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Two Things Worth Knowing Before You Decide</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Both were blocked from selling in Turkey.</strong> Turkey's telecom regulator (BTK) blocked Airalo's and Saily's websites and apps for purchases starting mid-2025, alongside several other eSIM providers. An eSIM from either one bought and installed before you land still works fine once you're there; the block only stops you from buying or topping up while physically inside the country.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Saily has a subscription tier Airalo doesn't really have an equivalent for.</strong> Saily Ultra ($59.99/month) bundles 30GB of high-speed data across 121+ destinations, the full NordVPN/NordPass/NordLayer/Incogni suite, 8% cashback in Saily credit, and a monthly airport lounge pass plus fast-track security pass. It's a real deal for someone who travels constantly and would otherwise pay for the VPN suite separately; a bad one for an occasional traveler who just needs data for a single trip.
  </p>
  <p>
    For device setup and eSIM basics that apply to both providers, see our <a href="/compatible-devices/">eSIM compatible devices</a> guide.
  </p>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <h2>Airalo vs Saily FAQ</h2>
  <div class="content-faq">
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Which is cheaper, Airalo or Saily</h3>
      <p>Saily, slightly, across most destinations we checked: about 10-12% less per GB than Airalo before either discount code is applied.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Does Saily's bundled VPN actually matter</h3>
      <p>Only if you'd otherwise pay for one. Saily's ad blocking, malware/phishing blocking, and virtual-location tool are built into every plan at no extra cost. Airalo has no equivalent; you'd need a separate app for the same protection.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Can I use either one in Turkey</h3>
      <p>Yes, if you buy and install it before you land. Both Airalo's and Saily's sites and apps were blocked from new purchases and top-ups inside Turkey by the country's telecom regulator starting mid-2025, but an already-installed eSIM keeps working.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content-faq-item">
      <h3>Why does Airalo have so many different discount codes</h3>
      <p>Airalo runs a referral program (Airmoney) that gives every user their own personal $3-off code to share, instead of one central affiliate discount. Saily doesn't run that kind of program, which is why it has a single storewide code instead.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

